    Use one AudioRecord per VirtualDevice
    
    Instead of relying on 2 AudioRecords, one just for managing the audio
    policies and one for the actual audio data transfer, just reuse
    the first created AudioRecord (which is still always open/recording).
    This reduces mix recreation impact introduced by ag/27671536 under the
    com.android.media.audioserver.fix_input_sharing_logic flag.
    It also works as expected with and without the flag enabled.
    
    This practically fixes the audio playback restart after pause on/from
    a remote virtual device. Using a manual flush on the always running AudioRecord, the stream is now playing on the client device with no glitches when pausing a playback.
    
    Bug: 358151598
    Test: From VdmHost app (with audio client setting enabled) create a
    virtual device on a client with audio capabilities. Play an audio stream
    (e.g. local host media files in the Files app) and pause and unpause the
    playback.
