    cargo_embargo: Add dirgroup for Trusty soong build
    
    For AVF, Trusty will also be built with soong to be run on the VM.
    To reference Trusty dependencies, Android.bp should define dirgroup.
    
    Here's the sample outputs from /external/rust/crates/acpi where Android.bp
    doesn't exist.
    
    ```
    // This file is generated by cargo_embargo.
    // Do not modify this file because the changes will be overridden on upgrade.
    
    package {
        default_applicable_licenses: ["external_rust_crates_acpi_license"],
        default_team: "trendy_team_android_rust",
    }
    
    license {
        name: "external_rust_crates_acpi_license",
        visibility: [":__subpackages__"],
        license_kinds: ["SPDX-license-identifier-Apache-2.0"],
        license_text: ["LICENSE"],
    }
    
    dirgroup {
        name: "trusty_dirgroup_external_rust_crates_acpi",
        visibility: ["//trusty/vendor/google/aosp/scripts"],
        dirs: ["."],
    }
    ```
    
    Bug: 372642893
    Test: Run cargo_embargo generate cargo_embargo.json
    Change-Id: I4eeb3ce249edc16cc9d26ed86940908158183f03

