    Add ManagedCrate struct, with major refactoring.
    
    Ensure that whenever we update or regenerate a crate, the vendored
    version we pick matches what's in pseudo_crate/Cargo.toml. Fixing
    this bug was the original goal of this change, but doing so proved to be
    a good reason to do some much-needed refactoring and simplification:
    
    * Get rid of VersionMatch. It was useful for the initial stages of the
      migration, but was unnecessarily complicated because logic for copying
      Android customizations, applying patches, and running cargo_embargo
      was scattered across VersionMatch, migration.rs, and CrateType.
    * Instead, introduce a ManagedCrate struct, which contains much of the
      same logic, with a better API.
    * CrateType is now much simpler. Basically just a convenience wrapper
      for a path and a parsed manifest file.
    * Add type state logic to PseudoCrate, to ensure that we know whether
      the Cargo.toml has been modified, in which case we need to re-run
      cargo vendor.
    
    I ran the following commands manually to test that everything is still
    working as expected:
    
    ```
    ./android_cargo.py run --bin crate_health -- help
    
    ./android_cargo.py run --bin crate_health -- --verbose migration-health aarch64-paging
    ./android_cargo.py run --bin crate_health -- --verbose migration-health bytemuck
    ./android_cargo.py run --bin crate_health -- --verbose migration-health drm-ffi
    ./android_cargo.py run --bin crate_health -- --verbose migration-health mockall_derive
    ./android_cargo.py run --bin crate_health -- --verbose migration-health jni
    
    ./android_cargo.py run --bin crate_health -- migrate codespan-reporting
    
    ./android_cargo.py run --bin crate_health -- regenerate ahash
    ./android_cargo.py run --bin crate_health -- regenerate hashbrown
    ./android_cargo.py run --bin crate_health -- regenerate httparse
    
    ./android_cargo.py run --bin crate_health -- regenerate-all
    
    ./android_cargo.py run --bin crate_health -- fix-licenses
    
    ./android_cargo.py run --bin crate_health -- fix-metadata
    ```
    
    Bug: http://b/339424309
