    remerge3: Redo 3-way merge for files with conflict markers
    
    This tool is useful when one developer uploads a merge commit with
    conflict markers, and another developer can fetch and amend the merge
    commit with 3-way merge tools.
    Supports bcompare, meld and vimdiff.
    
    Usage:
    1. Developer 1 does `git merge` and resolve any conflicts by checking in
       the conflict markers verbatim. (diff3 style merker is preferred)
       ```
       git config --global merge.conflictstyle diff3
       # Just mark the conflicting files as "resolved"
       git merge / git add . / git merge --continue / git merge --commit
       repo upload
       ```
    
    2. Developer 2 fetches the merge commit (with bad merge result) uploaded
       by developer 1 and run remerge3 to redo 3-way merge for files with
       conflict markers.
       ```
       alias remerge3=${ANDROID_TOP}/development/tools/mergetool/remerge3.sh
       git fetch / git checkout <merge commit>
       # Find all files with conflict markers and redo merge
       remerge3
       # Or specify a list of files to remerge
       remerge3 FILE1 [FILE2...]
       # Amend with good merge result and upload
       git commit --amend / repo upload
       ```
    
    Test: remerge3 [-h] [-t {bcompare,meld,vimdiff}]
    Change-Id: Ief25e42879a51919b3a197cd49f9140f366ea7d3

