    Do not literally compare referenced_type of class fields
    
    referenced_type is a mangled name and an optional suffix that
    distinguishes multiple definitions. header-abi-linker does not always
    generate deterministic referenced_type for multiple definitions and
    anonymous types. When header-abi-diff checks class, struct, or union
    fields, it should not literally compare the referenced_types. It looks
    up the TypeIRs and compares the attributes.
    
    Bug: 355612961
    Test: ANDROID_BUILD_TOP=`realpath .` \
          PATH=$PATH:`realpath out/soong/dist/bin` \
          development/vndk/tools/header-checker/tests/test.py
