    ViewerInput: Show rects with input windows when SF trace available
    
    - Parse input windows directly from the SurfaceFlinger trace
    - Store input windows as 'secondaryRects' in HierarchyTreeNode
    - Introduce new 'isSpy' property to TraceRect, which will indicate
      whether the input window is a spy window
    - Introduce a RectsComponent inside ViewerInput that only shows up when
      there is a corresponding SF trace
    - Display the input windows that correspond to the selected input event
      in the RectsComponent
      - If an input window is a target of the selected event, the window
        will be marked as 'hasContent', and will thus be drawn in a
        different color
      - If an input window is a spy window, it will be drawn with a low
        opacity so that we can see windows behind it more easily because
        touches would go through these spy windows
      - Double clicking a rect will open the corresponding entry in the SF
        viewer tab to make it easy to look up details about the window
    - Add user options for the RectsComponent to allow showing only visible
      windows and only showing windows that is the target of the current
      event (hasContent)
    
