    Speed up ViewerTransactions initialization
    
    Reduce initialization time by 20% querying all the Transactions
    trace entries at once with Promise.all().
    
    Promise.all() helps to hide TP latency and the profiling
    shows that now we are spending only ~5% of the time waiting
    for TP. Most of the time (~60%) is spent transforming the fake
    protos. Meaning we could get a significant speed up querying
    non-transformed protos from the Trace object, i.e. querying
    custom data (b/291213403).
    
    Note that now we are loading all the Transactions trace entries
    into memory. This will increase memory pressure, but shouldn't
    be an issue as the Transactions trace is quite lightweight
    compared to SurfaceFlinger (layers) and WindowManager (windows).
    
    Bug: b/299425256
    Test: npm run test:presubmit
    Change-Id: Ib079c74700892edb72cec045e82fbfd709236ec6

