    Fix handling of dumps with invalid timestamps
    
    Dumps with invalid timestamps (value 0) are filtered out
    from TimelineData, otherwise they would mess up the timeline
    presentation. In some cases this could prevent TracePipeline to
    retrieve (through TimelineData) a TracePosition to be used
    for viewers initialization. E.g. viewers would remain
    uninitialized when only dump traces were loaded.
    
    This commit handles the corner case in which only dump traces
    with invalid timestamps are loaded. With this change TracePipeline
    falls back to pick any timestamp from the loaded traces and uses
    it for viewers initialization.
    
    Bug: 262243662
    Test: npm run test:presubmit
    Change-Id: Id22e3679c4d3308867a44962ff67682df16cb3dd

